  - scintigraphy
abstract: >-
  A package format that turns one medical image into a self-describing directory a vision-language model can read
  zero-shot: a schema-validated manifest with assertion levels, model-ready renders, tool-computed measurements with
  provenance, and a fixed-template natural-language reference file. Includes the reference converter, the CLI and SDK,
  and OIP-Bench, a benchmark of image-understanding tasks with frozen replies from eleven models.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Open Image Protocol: self-describing medical image packages supply the facts vision-language models cannot see in an image, but not the check against the pixels"
  authors:
